  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Just had an idea since a group of mine is currently being targeted by a bunch of Crashers and client users.\n\nSince easy anti cheat seems to be useless in this situation.\n\nWhat if there's a random scan while the game is active maybe while World switching where the game will check and see if there's any modifications to its files at all and if there is a single modification then it closes.\n\nAll this should affect is loading time if it happens during a world switch and if implemented correctly it shouldn't be easily bypassed like easy anti cheat.\n\nDoesn't do much for the Crasher avatars but it will make modding a little more annoying.\n\nEdit- this part is more targeting Crasher avatars. We already have the ability to automatically block avatars based on their optimization levels however most avatars are poorly optimized nowadays since the parameters for a poorly optimized Avatar are honestly quite low. What if avatars were automatically blocked by default if they meet certain criteria like a certain amount of particles or meshes to help prevent particle crashes or mesh crashes? Just an idea.",
